            <ArticleTitle>Restenosis due to underexpansion of sirolimus-eluting stent in a bifurcation lesion.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>496-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Even in the drug-eluting stent era, percutaneous coronary intervention in bifurcation lesions is complex and technically demanding, and considerable expertise is required. This case report describes in-stent restenosis due to stent underexpansion after kissing stents using sirolimus-eluting stents.</AbstractText>
